        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "It was a rainy day, but the excitement of over 20 tourists at Singapore’s Fort Canning Tree Tunnel was sky-high. Most of them were from China. Among them was 25-year-old Liu Meifeng. She was "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "eagerly",
            "ref": "v-eagerly"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " waiting for her turn to "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pose",
            "zh": "摆姿势"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for photos. It was her first visit to Singapore. She discovered the place through "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "recommendations",
            "ref": "v-recommendation"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on Xiaohongshu."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "As one of the top social media platforms in China these days, Xiaohongshu has turned some lesser-known places into must-see attractions. The Fort Canning Tree Tunnel is just one example. While it’s well-known among professional nature photographers, locals don’t usually think of it as a tourist destination. Liu loved the place and called Xiaohongshu her tour guide. After taking her pictures, she "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "posted",
            "ref": "v-post"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " them on the app to share with this growing community."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Vissy Chow was also in the long line. The tree tunnel was the first stop on her very first visit to Singapore. The 20-year-old was also following a recommended route on Xiaohongshu. “It’s not that nice, but since I’m here, I "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "might as well",
            "ref": "v-might-as-well"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " join the line for some shots,” she said."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Just one subway stop away, a few other Chinese tourists were posing in front of the Old Hill Street Police Station. The facility is also "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "featured",
            "ref": "v-feature"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in many Xiaohongshu posts. People call it the “Rainbow Police Station” because of its colourful windows."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Eleven-year-old Amy Lee was in the crowd with her mother. Earlier that day, they had visited the National Gallery. “If you go there, you will see lots of Chinese tourists,” said the mother. “With Xiaohongshu, we don’t need guides anymore. We know exactly where to ‘"
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "da ka"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "’ (check in)!”"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
